./docs/plans/evidence/brain-w27-temporal/context-capture.json:2274:        "markdown": "## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`\n\nI'm Rowan. Vik knows me as Rowan, and that's how I know myself here. Codex is\nthe runtime I work through.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:0:f1c660caa96d5b28`\n- roles: `identity`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik.md`\n\nWork with Vik as a direct, mechanism-led thought partner. Challenge weak\nreasoning, follow Grice, assume technical ability, and optimize attention.\nDiscuss required changes only; lead with mechanism, expected result, next step.\n\nBring the expertise the problem needs without waiting for Vik to name the role.\nDo not let Codex's software-development context turn every problem into a\nsoftware problem.\n\nMake the practical value of a recommendation clear; technical interest alone\nis not leverage.\n\nBefore recommending, designing, or building around a product capability,\nestablish and state whether Vik can actually use it. Check the relevant plan,\nbilling mode, account or workspace role, region, rollout or preview status,\nand feature gates before implementation. Protocol, schema, implementation, or\nrelease-note presence proves that a capability exists, not that Vik is entitled\nto it. If access is unknown, label the recommendation conditional and verify\neligibility first.\n\nWhen Vik introduces a bounded method that materially improves equivalent work,\ngeneralize it across the remaining equivalent decisions without waiting for\nhim to repeat the instruction. Keep ownership of scope, synthesis, judgment,\nand the conversation; stop generalizing when the method stops being useful or\nthe work is no longer genuinely equivalent.\n\nIf Vik asks me to pause, stop and leave the work in a state we can resume.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:1:32f468d2171eded0`\n- roles: `collaboration`\n\n#### `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is my maintained cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:7ad5c9c076c4c717`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `work-history/brain-context-runtime.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAnvil now injects a bounded Brain bootstrap at Codex SessionStart instead of only pointing the model toward a later manual bootstrap call.\n\nThe runtime:\n\n- loads the ordered core identity and collaboration pages from `brain-bootstrap.json`;\n- matches a known workspace to its Brain project page by normalized git remote before directory alias;\n- keeps unknown projects explicit rather than substituting an unrelated project page;\n- uses the Brain-local canonical llm-wiki compiler for supporting context;\n- validates compiler envelopes and real selected paths before reading page bodies;\n- caps rendered Brain Markdown by UTF-8 bytes and emits stable degraded diagnostics;\n- preserves Continuity first, keeps startup non-blocking, and provides an emergency Brain-only bypass.\n\nThe installed SessionStart command now calls the unified `anvil codex context-hook`; the previous `session-start-hook` name remains a compatibility alias for this rollout slice.\n\nThe later prompt-time slices are recorded separately in\n[Prompt-Specific Brain Recall](./work-history/brain-prompt-recall.md) and\n[Unified Agent Skills Prompt Hook](./work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md).\n\nTask 6 then established Brain as the sole durable owner of detailed global\ncollaboration doctrine, shrank the global instructions to a small bootstrap,\nand migrated four separately reviewed native-memory profile rules into\n[Working With Vik](./self-model/working-with-vik.md). The approved private Git\nidentity remains inside Brain; the public Anvil review records only its\nredacted meaning.\n\nTask 7 completed the runtime cutover. Codex native memory remains enabled and\nits local store remains intact, but automatic native-memory injection is now\ndisabled with `memories.use_memories = false`. Anvil's bounded `Brain Recall`\nhook remains active, so Brain is now the only durable cognition automatically\nrecalled by this user-owned runtime layer while Continuity still supplies hot\nworking state.\n\nThe 2026-07-16 standing-guidance follow-up closes the ordinary-prompt clarity\ngap without manipulating retrieval queries. The optional version 1 manifest\nextension declares a compact subset of core pages plus a dedicated hard byte\nlimit. On every `UserPromptSubmit`, Anvil validates and renders that guidance\nfirst, runs the existing exact-prompt llm-wiki recall once, removes duplicate\nguidance selections, and preserves the existing total prompt cap. Old\nmanifests remain valid with standing guidance disabled. The canonical\n[Working With Vik](./self-model/working-with-vik.md) page is now compact;\ntask-specific rules remain durable on its linked situational page rather than\nbeing injected into every turn.\n\nThe 2026-07-18 repair exposed a maintenance gap. Brain already described Anvil\nas producing excellent working systems, but the compact standing page omitted\nthe explicit production-grade foundation rule. Adding it without compiling the\nreal standing section then grew that section from 2,939 to 3,343 bytes, beyond\nthe reviewed 3,072-byte limit, so prompt recall degraded. The standing page was\ncompacted without weakening the rule, and Brain lint now mirrors Anvil's\nfrontmatter stripping, section rendering, and UTF-8 byte measurement.\n\n- evidence_id: `text:work-history/brain-context-runtime.md#What Changed`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/manifest-production-shaping.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What Changed\n\nVik and Rowan shaped [Manifest](./entities/manifest.md) from a recurring\ncross-stack failure mode: organic work branches faster than flat plans and\ncompact session memory can preserve it. A static concept probe established that\na work graph, active frontier, and append-only history matched the lived need.\n\nVik accepted Manifest as Anvil's native cross-project work substrate and\napproved its production vocabulary: Ledger, Current, Frontier, Chronicle, and\nAgent Context. Manifest remains observational and state-bearing in v0; it does\nnot assign, dispatch, schedule, or orchestrate agents.\n\nThe accepted contract keeps Manifest separate from\n[Continuity](./entities/continuity.md), treats markdown plans as linked\nnarrative evidence rather than future operational task truth, and requires\nhistorical imports to preserve uncertainty without silently activating work.\n\nVik also made [Anvil MCP](./entities/anvil-mcp.md) the default operational\nadapter for agent-facing Anvil capabilities. The accepted boundary keeps domain\nsemantics and state in host-neutral service cores while MCP exposes bounded,\ntyped operations. Hooks supply trusted lifecycle provenance; CLI remains the\noperator and recovery surface; skills guide workflows; UIs serve humans.\n\nVik then rejected \"smallest trustworthy\" as the implementation target. The\ncorrected plan withdraws the JSONL-first default, adds a carrier qualification\ntask before storage, and makes the production readiness gate part of the same\nphase rather than later hardening.\n\nTwo opposite paths were rejected. Building a minimum foundation and hardening\nit later would let dogfood state make a temporary carrier permanent before its\nfailure model was designed. Building the complete future roadmap would confuse\nproduction quality with speculative scope. The accepted correction applies the\nquality bar to included capabilities while leaving import, UI, sync, and\norchestration for separate evidence and approval.\n\nThe final plan review found a remaining contradiction: Manifest became the sole\ntask authority before its doctor, backup, restore, migration, and readiness\nproof were complete. Vik approved a two-stage correction. A fresh-host native\ntrial may mirror real work after the MCP surface exists, but it remains\nnon-authoritative. Only after the complete readiness gate passes may the trial\nbe reconciled, agent instructions change, and Manifest take operational\nauthority.\n\nThe same correction makes backup/export, restore, and schema migration explicit\noperator commands with dry-run and deliberate apply paths. It also gives the\nManifest tools a focused MCP adapter for schemas, handlers, and registration,\nleaving the shared server as composition and the host-neutral core free of MCP\nSDK types.\n\nTasks 0 through 8 then implemented the qualified SQLite carrier, strict domain\ncontracts, hash-chained production Ledger, deterministic projections,\nintent-shaped service, bounded Agent Context, focused MCP adapter, and trusted\nhost binding. The original ten MCP tools became twelve when the native trial\nshowed that honest evolution and correction of a wrong claim required distinct\ntyped operations.\n\nTask 9 completed through the real Codex host on 2026-07-20. The trial tracked\nthree branching cross-project threads, preserved an evidence-backed correction\nand later reframe, completed resolved work, retired its blocker, and read back\nthe active and historical views with trusted Work Context provenance. The\ntrial remains non-authoritative.\n\nTask 10 completed on 2026-07-20. Human operators can now inspect Current,\nFrontier, and Chronicle through concise output or stable JSON, and run a\nstrictly read-only doctor that distinguishes failure classes and reports exact\nrecovery boundaries without initializing, repairing, migrating, or removing\nlocks. The CLI adds no mutation surface; agents continue to write through\ntrusted MCP.\n\nThe tracked Brain compiler repair discovered during current-status retrieval\nthen completed\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `text:work-history/manifest-production-shaping.md#What Changed`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/manifest-production-shaping.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nAnvil is moving beyond work that fits neatly inside one repository or one\nagent session. Loci language resolution, Brain evidence work, and Manifest\nitself already demonstrate causal branches, blockers, return points, and\ncross-project relationships that can disappear when task state is split across\nplans, chats, and memory frames.\n\nManifest gives that work one durable substrate without forcing organic\ndevelopment into a rigid queue. The MCP-first rule also prevents each new Anvil\ncapability from inventing a different agent integration while avoiding the\nopposite mistake of coupling capability logic to the MCP server.\n\nDogfooding still proves real use, but trial and authority are no longer the same\nevent. The non-authoritative trial proves workflow behavior; the later cutover\nchanges task authority only after operational recovery and readiness are real.\n\nThe completed trial also proved that Manifest can learn from real organic work\nwithout rewriting history: a wrong claim is corrected with later evidence,\nwhile genuinely evolved work is reframed as a separate event.\n\nT10 makes that graph operable by a human without weakening its authority\nboundary. Operators can see work and diagnose whether recovery is needed, but\ndiagnosis cannot silently change the Ledger or compete with MCP mutation.\n\nT11 makes the work graph recoverable and gives its complete service an honest\nproduction boundary. It corrects the tempting but false equivalence between a\ndatabase physically holding one million representative events and the current\nservice processing that history interactively. That correction keeps the\nquality claim measurable and gives larger scale a concrete indexed expansion\npath rather than an emergency bypass.\n\nT12 turns that qualified capability into the shared working substrate. Organic\nbranches can now survive repository and session boundaries in one accepted\nstate graph, while the user and live evidence remain authoritative over what\nthe graph should say.\n\nThe adoption correction makes that result operational rather than aspirational:\nfresh Anvil-enabled Codex sessions receive the authority rule before tool\ndiscovery, and humans can inspect the same shared graph through one installed\ncommand from any repository.\n\nThe visual dashboard makes the organic shape of that graph understandable to\nVik without asking him to reconstruct it from CLI rows. Keeping it read-only\npreserves one operational authority while still giving the human side a live\nview of branches, blockers, return paths, evidence, and complete history.\n\n- evidence_id: `text:work-history/manifest-production-shaping.md#Why It Mattered`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Global Codex collaboration reconciliation](./sources/global-codex-collaboration-reconciliation-2026-07-14.md)\n- Anvil commit `9d86f6c` records the approved Task 6 instruction ownership inventory.\n- Anvil commit `cb59b94` records the approved global shrink and its runtime proof.\n- Pre-shrink global instruction hash:\n  `cc138760864a6f46fba8f99de185563b277e35a31ba9a8bedcf4d8fb70a7d51e`.\n- A restricted-`PATH` SessionStart probe exited successfully with 21,939 bytes,\n  below the 24,576-byte hard cap, and contained both new rules.\n- A fresh `codex exec --ephemeral --sandbox read-only` process used normal hook\n  trust, completed one `UserPromptSubmit` hook, and returned exactly the two\n  expected behaviors without using tools: distinguish known, inferred, and\n  still-unproven claims; inspect available files, thread, context, and repository\n  before asking Vik.\n- Brain lint and render passed after the reconciliation.\n- Post-shrink global bootstrap hash:\n  `3dc45def9f133c4be36f8011cdf798136d3f1fb5caafae4cec062c922d3fcc44`.\n- The healthy restricted-`PATH` SessionStart route emitted 21,929 bytes,\n  included Rowan's Brain, and did not report degradation.\n- A direct missing-agent hook probe emitted `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`,\n  `status: degraded`, and no Rowan content.\n- A fresh normal Codex process named the Anvil-injected Brain as canonical,\n  named current instructions and live evidence as the override, and stated the\n  reviewed missing-context behavior.\n- A fresh process with `ANVIL_BRAIN_CONTEXT=off` reported Brain unavailable,\n  used only current instructions and live evidence, and refused to reconstruct\n  Brain from memory.\n- A fresh\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `text:work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md#Evidence`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n### Diagnostics\n\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_HISTORY_INVALID\n- message: Authored temporal history is invalid; its prose cannot supply a settled answer: entities/anvil-mcp.md, entities/brain.md, entities/codex.md (+15 more)\n- recovery: Repair the affected authored history through the wiki Steward; do not use its prose as a settled temporal answer.\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_UNCERTAIN\n- message: Relevant context has no verified claim for the requested time or has unspecified temporal state: entities/anvil-primitives.md, entities/continuity.md, entities/go.md (+31 more)\n- recovery: Use explicit temporal or source follow-up before claiming current or dated applicability; do not invent missing times.\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `work-history/brain-context-runtime.md`, `work-history/manifest-production-shaping.md`, `work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md`\n- temporal_query: {\"view\":\"current\",\"request_time\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:21.695000Z\",\"world_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:21.695000Z\",\"known_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:21.695000Z\"}\n",
