./AGENTS.md-87-- Read continuity when orientation matters, the current frame is uncertain, or a session/work boundary needs recovery.
./AGENTS.md-88-- When accepted work must survive a conversation boundary, use `anvil_continuity_checkpoint_task` to set or replace the singular active task, mark it waiting, or clear it when no work remains. Supply a retry-stable checkpoint id, update the checkpoint whenever the task or next step changes, and verify the returned rendered frame before ending the turn.
./AGENTS.md-89-- Use `anvil_continuity_record_event`, `anvil_continuity_promote_event`, and `anvil_continuity_retire_projection_item` for durable signals outside the active task. The repo CLI is acceptable for continuity `read`, `doctor`, and `init-default`, but not as the discovery path for mutation. If the required MCP mutation tool is unavailable, stop and report the missing MCP surface instead of probing or inventing a CLI mutation path.
./AGENTS.md:90:- Work Context binding ids and mutation routing are supplied by the host adapter. Do not invent a binding id, reuse one from another session, or pass a repository path to make it the Continuity owner.
./AGENTS.md-91-- Record a continuity event when durable non-task signal emerges: an approved decision, open question, correction, phase change, repeated failure mode, or capability change.
./AGENTS.md-92-- Promote a recorded event only when it should appear in the compact injected frame for future sessions.
./AGENTS.md-93-- Treat the compact injected frame as the current working set. If promotion fails because a projection list is full, retire the least-current compact item with a correction event, then promote the current signal. Prefer evicting historical implementation notes before active decisions, current next actions, accepted working examples, or live open questions. Retiring a projection item must not delete event history.
